// Title: Turla Group Commands May 2020
// Sigma ID: 9e2e51c5-c699-4794-ba5a-29f5da40ac0c
// Status: test | Level: critical
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2020-05-26 | Modified: 2025-10-19
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, stealth, G0010, execution, T1059.001, T1053.005, T1027
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects commands used by Turla group as reported by ESET in May 2020
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.welivesecurity.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/ESET_Turla_ComRAT.pdf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-emerging-threats/2014/TA/Turla/proc_creation_win_apt_turla_comrat_may20.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "tracert -h 10 yahoo.com" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".WSqmCons))|iex;" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Fr`omBa`se6`4Str`ing") or (ProcessCommandLine matches regex "net\\s+use\\s+https://docs.live.net" and ProcessCommandLine contains "@aol.co.uk")
